":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-7-4-18"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"7004018","sanskritFile":"Ram07.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"97a84cc26360d0a37ed13f66c460e17f010b916ee9886d7db65d449617c2dad6","compact":"d8305fc38977829fe214cf6442cd2323a9f1268a58802b90440d7ba6a4d5a747","nasal":"6175d849092487f85678519ebfc89d484c85af3f43c642ccf30f1c243981fa0d"}},{"id":"VRCE-7-4-19","kanda":7,"kandaId":"uttara","sarga":4,"verse":19,"english":"And when that night-ranger arrived at proper youth, his sire turned his attention towards his marriage.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-7-4-19"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"7004019","sanskritFile":"Ram07.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"803e222eb250b292326d7082a4d5048c6a23b0b9efd1468e8c99a42b26f86f53","compact":"5e3eaef092c00a89f682f26ba339def8d591a39a2886b57b6169a97e270b0621","nasal":"5e3eaef092c00a89f682f26ba339def8d591a39a2886b57b6169a97e270b0621"}},{"id":"VRCE-7-4-20","kanda":7,"kandaId":"uttara","sarga":4,"verse":20,"english":"And that best of Rākṣasas-heti-in the interests of his son asked for the hand of Sandhya's daughter; like to Sandhyā* herself in the potency. * The evening Twilight-spouse of the Sun.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.81,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-7-4-20"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"7004020","sanskritFile":"Ram07.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"ef15c2fc3a2fb2569da9df6330e3d054c296846a094526b7e381d4a8d3355ed2","compact":"565861117f2e89a9f5ec8bf0d710b54bf6cb55d2d2f51ebf4d40c0e691c91ba3","nasal":"565861117f2e89a9f5ec8bf0d710b54bf6cb55d2d2f51ebf4d40c0e691c91ba3"}},{"id":"VRCE-7-4-21","kanda":7,"kandaId":"uttara","sarga":4,"verse":21,"english":"Sandhya, reflecting that she needs must have to be given away by her, bestowed her on Vidyutkesa, O Raghava. Having obtained Sandhya's daughter, the night-ranger Vidyutkeśa, sports with her even as Maghavan does with the daughter of Puloma.","alignment":{"type":"grouped","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-7-4-21"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"7004021","sanskritFile":"Ram07.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"613e7c2c2c871eaccf7c1c82fa9fb49b17238d54a29168b9edfe046855696bf7","compact":"0c79ca05d8435c427e7d842c9d346170e1ad26d46d70c20402f56ab0c139ae10","nasal":"b1155a3633889059071ff05538718a2de5f64d3445132218cfd768020c188fd8"}},{"id":"VRCE-7-4-22","kanda":7,"kandaId":"uttara","sarga":4,"verse":22,"english":"Sandhya, reflecting that she needs must have to be given away by her, bestowed her on Vidyutkesa, O Raghava. Having obtained Sandhya's daughter, the night-ranger Vidyutkeśa, sports with her even as Maghavan does with the daughter of Puloma.","alignment":{"type":"grouped","confidence":0.937,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-7-4-21"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"7004022","sanskritFile":"Ram07.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"18f73862dfbbb438b1d396d9a28e73bc237dd41ed077040d411c8fc0c0c3adaa","compact":"8edadd068613bc07fc1696ad2e44a65888bd99b9e9a505e78bc2e7b85a63816b","nasal":"8edadd068613bc07fc1696ad2e44a65888bd99b9e9a505e78bc2e7b85a63816b"}},{"id":"VRCE-7-4-23","kanda":7,"kandaId":"uttara","sarga":4,"verse":23,"english":"It came to pass that after a length of time, O Răma, Sälakatankata was filled with child by Vidyutkeśa, as the clouds are furnished with water by the Ocean,","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.864,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-7-4-22"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"7004023","sanskritFile":"Ram07.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"253e2072956313cf